# Motion

Animate with CSS in `utilities/_motion.scss` and the component partial that owns the element. Reach for JavaScript only when CSS cannot express the interaction.

Use `transform` and `opacity`. Duration tokens: `--duration-fast: 180ms`, `--duration-base: 280ms`, `--duration-slow: 560ms`. Easing: `--ease-out: cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1)`.

- Cards lift `4px` and deepen the shadow on hover.
- Buttons transition color and shadow. No bounce, elastic, or infinite loops.
- Drawers and the mini cart slide with `translateX` or `translateY`.
- Hero and product-grid entrance can stagger, capped at six children.
- `scroll-behavior: smooth` applies only when the shopper allows motion.

```scss
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
  .product-card {
    transition:
      transform var(--duration-base) var(--ease-out),
      box-shadow var(--duration-base) var(--ease-out);

    &:hover {
      transform: translateY(-4px);
    }
  }
}

@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  *,
  *::before,
  *::after {
    animation-duration: 0.01ms !important;
    animation-iteration-count: 1 !important;
    transition-duration: 0.01ms !important;
    scroll-behavior: auto !important;
  }
}
```
